Section: x11
Priority: optional
Description: HyprDebian desktop
 Depends on the packages of the HyprDebian desktop, so that they are
 installed with it and stay installed: Hyprland with uwsm, hyprpaper,
 hypridle, hyprlock, its dialogs and XWayland, greetd, the desktop portals,
 kitty, mako, PipeWire, the screenshot tools, the dark GTK theme, plymouth,
 and the desktop applications. HyprDebian installs no recommends, so these
 are all the packages the desktop needs. It depends on hd-base of the same
 version, the HyprDebian version of both.
 .
 greetd logs the first user in to Hyprland on tty7 at the boot; the user is
 the key hd-desktop of /etc/hyprdebian/config.json, written into
 /etc/greetd/config.toml by hd-desktop-render. The package also installs the
 files that new users get in /etc/skel: the configs of Hyprland, hypridle,
 hyprlock, hyprpaper, kitty, mako, mpv and PipeWire, and the
 commands that the key bindings run: the reboot and power off questions, the
 monitor mode menu, the mount menus and the volume keys. The users in the
 group sudo mount and unmount drives from the mount menus without a
 password.
 .
 It holds the parts of the desktop:
  - the Emerald wallpaper of Debian 12, in /usr/share/backgrounds/hyprdebian;
  - JetBrains Mono with the icons of Nerd Fonts, from the Nerd Fonts release
    v3.4.0, in /usr/share/fonts/truetype/jetbrains-mono-nerd;
  - hd-menu, the keyboard-driven menu, which reads a menu as JSON from stdin
    and prints the value of the option chosen;
  - the theme engine hd-theme, with the themes in /etc/hyprdebian/themes,
    the theme of the system in the key hd-theme of
    /etc/hyprdebian/config.json and the theme of a user in that key of
    ~/.config/hyprdebian/config.json;
  - the screensaver, a text with the random effects of terminal text effects
    on every monitor, which hypridle starts after 2 minutes;
  - the plymouth theme hyprdebian, which looks like the lock screen of
    hyprlock in the theme of the system, rendered by hd-plymouth-render, and
    asks for the password of an encrypted ZFS dataset. The package makes it
    the theme of plymouth and conflicts with desktop-base, whose themes it
    replaces.
 .
 hd-launcher-cache writes the menu of the application launcher, the input of
 hd-menu, from the .desktop files in /usr/share/applications, in
 /var/cache/hd-launcher for root and in ~/.cache/hd-launcher for other users,
 and prints it for the launcher; an apt hook writes the one of the system
 and those of the users in the group users each time apt has run dpkg.
